[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) was merged as one issue and marked known. It is not one issue. The
reports hold three different problems with three different fixes, so each has its own ticket.

<Callout>
Not known as one. Merging by subject line ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject))
put separate bugs into one ticket.
</Callout>

## The split

<ProblemSplit ticket={4471} {issues} />

- **parser** – the shared parser reads every date month first; tenants that write the day first get flipped dates.
- **hint** – the booking-v3 form prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under the date field, so day-first tenants type month first. Form channel only; fix the hint, not the parser.
- **oneDay** – dates off by exactly one day (a Tuesday shown as Monday, "only June", Lisbon and Toronto getting different days). That is not a swap. Timezone handling is the suspect.

## How the causes were told apart

The cause depends on the tenant's locale and booking form, not on intake's tag, which is only a
guess from the browser.

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

The one-day reports are counted under their tenant's cause above and footnoted there; they are
the third ticket.

## Lessons

- Intake's tag disagrees with the cause for many reports. Look up the tenant.
- A subject-line merge hides bugs that sound alike. Check the cause before you call a ticket known.

<RenderStamp {signature} />
